# task-flow: sync

**Prefer:** `@task-flow-sync` · Skill: `.claude/skills/task-flow-sync/workflow.md` · Works with `/task-flow-sync` and `task-flow: sync`.

## 1. Read

- `.task-flow/tasks.input.txt` (lines starting with `- ` only)
- `.task-flow/.internal/tasks.json`, `status.json` if they exist
- List `.task-flow/contexts/` for matching references

## 2. Diff by `originalRequest`

| Change | Action |
|--------|--------|
| **New** | Generate task + 3–8 subtasks; all `pending` |
| **Removed** | Drop from `tasks.json` + `status.json` (then `render-status` re-renders `tasks.status.md`) |
| **Modified** | Update title/description; regen subtasks; **preserve** done/pending/**manual** status where possible |
| **Unchanged** | Leave task data and status as-is |

Task IDs stay sequential (1, 2, 3…) matching `tasks.input.txt` order.

## 3. New / regenerated subtasks

- `originalRequest`: exact input line; `createdAt`: ISO 8601 for new tasks
- 3–8 subtasks: title, description, instructions (3–5 steps)
- `dependsOn`: set to the ids of other tasks this one genuinely needs done first (shared file/module, consumes something the other creates) — **not** just its position in `tasks.input.txt`. Leave empty when tasks are independent, even if listed sequentially. Re-evaluate it on every regen (a modified task's real dependencies can change).
- Contexts: keyword match or `task-flow-screen file.ext` → `.task-flow/contexts/file.ext`
- Subtask instructions: **checklist** in [coding_standards.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/coding_standards.mdc) only — not [coding-standards-full.md](mdc:.task-flow/guides/coding-standards-full.md)
- More templates: [task_generation.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/task_generation.mdc)

**Sync rules:** no codebase exploration; no questions.

## 4. Align status

- `status.json` = source of truth
- Run `rbin-task-flow render-status` to rebuild `tasks.status.md` (checkboxes `[ ]`/`[x]`/`[~]` + 📊 Summary: completed / in progress / 🖐️ manual / remaining + `🤖 AI N available` on parallel-ready tasks, from `dependsOn`) deterministically from `tasks.json` + `status.json` — do not hand-write it
- After regen: new subtasks → `pending`; keep `done` and `manual` on matched subtasks when possible

## 5. Principles

> Preserve progress when possible. Fast: read → diff → write. User runs `task-flow: status` or `@task-flow-run` next.
